's lean, the national environment, Powell's money advantage, and a 10-point polling average all point the same direction, and every major rater and market treats this as a Democratic pickup. The main caution is thin polling and a credible Republican nominee in a district that has historically swung with Bacon at the top of the ticket.", "watch": "A late shift in the national environment or a strong debate performance by Harding could narrow the margin enough to put the seat back in play.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Don Bacon (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Nebraska's 2nd District is an open seat after Republican Don Bacon's retirement, and Democrats are positioned to flip it. The district leans Democratic by about three points, and the 2026 environment adds to that advantage. Denise Powell has out-raised Brinker Harding and benefits from roughly $3 million in outside support, while super PACs have reportedly pulled back spending on the Republican side. Polls show Powell ahead by double digits, though the polling record is thin. Prediction markets uniformly give Powell about a 94% chance, and expert raters overwhelmingly call the race a likely or safe Democratic flip. Harding remains a serious candidate in a district that has often been competitive, but the weight of the evidence points to a comfortable Democratic win.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9278, "margin": 8.8}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9035, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.914, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9146, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8905, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9055, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.902, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8848, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9024, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9327, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9296, "margin": 8.5}, {